{"study_accession":"PRJNA1192416","secondary_study_accession":"SRP548490","title":"Detecting ceRNAs Associated with Dust Mite-Sensitized in the Whole Transcriptome of Allergic Rhinitis Human Peripheral blood mononuclear cell","description":"Allergic rhinitis is a difficult-to-cure allergic disease that occurs in the nasal cavity, and its pathogenesis remains unclear. In recent years, there has been growing interest in the role of non-coding RNAs. The use of transcriptome analysis techniques to study gene expression at the RNA level is important for in-depth study of disease pathogenesis. Therefore, we conducted whole-transcriptome sequencing on 5 healthy individuals and 5 Dust Mite-Sensitized of allergic rhinitis (22-88 years old). Analyzing mRNA and nonconding RNA expression, we constructed a ceRNA network and selecting 16 differentially expressed noncoding RNA validated by qRT-PCR. Its clinical significance was further investigated.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN45108560","study_accession":"PRJNA1192416","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-12-01","attributes":[["isolate","RNA"],["age","23"],["biomaterial_provider","PI"],["collection_date","2022-02-16"],["geo_loc_name","China"],["sex","female"],["tissue","blood"],["disease","allergic rhinitis"],["health_state","allergic rhinitis"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR31558474","experiment_accession":"SRX26924394","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"Oligo-dT","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":41633153,"base_count":12489945900,"first_public":"2024-12-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: allergic rhinitis, A"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN45108561","study_accession":"PRJNA1192416","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sa